# Architecture — spec section → code

Traceability map from the Master Build Specification to the implementation.
Nothing here is a standalone script: every capability plugs into the Section 2
architecture as an agent, a graph node or a knowledge-repository extension
(Section 18).

---

## Section 2 — System architecture

```
frontend/*.html  (plain HTML/CSS/JS)
        │
        ▼
backend/main.py + backend/api/*        FastAPI orchestration layer
        │
        ▼
backend/graphs/*                       LangGraph workflows (checkpointed)
backend/core/llm.py                    LangChain → Azure OpenAI (prompts/RAG only)
        │
        ▼
backend/agents/*                       16 agents
        │
        ▼
backend/knowledge/* + backend/core/vectorstore.py     SQLite (in-process cosine search)
        │
        ▼
java-framework/                        pure-Java Selenium-Cucumber, local jars
        │
        ▼
Edge + WebDriver + CDP  ·  backend/execution/socket_client.py (CBS)
        │
        ▼
backend/reporting/*                    interactive HTML reports
```

**Python orchestrates. Java executes.** The only place Python touches a browser
is the recorder (`backend/recorder/cdp_recorder.py`), which exists to *learn* the
application. Execution itself is always handed to the Java framework.

