## Section 3 — Technology stack

| Layer | Where |
|---|---|
| FastAPI orchestration | `backend/main.py`, `backend/api/` |
| LangGraph workflows | `backend/graphs/{recording,execution,brd}_graph.py` |
| LangChain (prompts / RAG / tool-calling only) | `backend/core/llm.py`, `backend/knowledge/rag.py` |
| Azure OpenAI (sole provider) | `backend/core/llm.py` — `get_chat_model`, `get_embeddings` |
| Edge + WebDriver + CDP | `backend/recorder/cdp_recorder.py`, `java-framework/.../DriverFactory.java` |
| Pure-Java build, no Maven/Gradle | `java-framework/build.{sh,bat}`, `backend/codegen/compiler.py` |
| Plain HTML/CSS/JS frontend | `frontend/` — no framework, no build step |
| SQLite (Python stdlib `sqlite3`) | `db/schema.sql`, `backend/core/db.py` |
| In-process vector search (JSON-encoded embeddings, brute-force cosine) | `knowledge_embeddings` table, `backend/core/vectorstore.py` |
| Encrypted secrets | `backend/core/security.py` (Fernet), `secrets` table |
| HTML reports | `backend/reporting/` |

DB, browser and file operations are done directly in Python — never through a
LangChain tool, exactly as the spec requires.

