## Section 8 — Framework Indexing Engine

`backend/framework_index/`

- `java_parser.py` — javalang with a regex fallback, so indexing works even if
  the wheel is unavailable. Extracts packages, classes, methods, annotations,
  Gherkin patterns, `@FindBy` and `By.*` locators.
- `indexer.py` — classifies every file (feature / page object / step definition /
  runner / utility / hook / property / test data), persists to
  `framework_artifacts`, `framework_methods`, `framework_relations`, and embeds
  each artefact for RAG.

Query helpers used by the Framework Search Agent: `find_artifacts`,
`find_step_definition`, `find_method`, `find_utilities`, `dependency_graph`.

---

## Section 9 — Knowledge retrieval

`backend/knowledge/rag.py :: build_context()` assembles, before every LLM call:
existing framework artefacts, the known transaction record, the locator
repository, recent execution history and past AI decisions (so the platform does
not repeat a known failure). If the SQLite database is unreachable it degrades
gracefully rather than hanging.

