## Section 10 — Agents

`backend/agents/__init__.py :: REGISTRY` — 16 singletons:

| Agent | Module |
|---|---|
| Recorder | `recorder_agent.py` |
| BRD | `brd_agent.py` |
| Knowledge | `knowledge_agent.py` |
| Framework Search | `framework_search_agent.py` |
| Locator | `locator_agent.py` |
| Test Data | `test_data_agent.py` |
| Feature Generation / Page Object / Step Definition / Test Runner / CodeGen | `codegen_agents.py` |
| Compilation | `compilation_agent.py` |
| Execution | `execution_agent.py` |
| Self-Healing | `self_heal_agent.py` |
| Report | `report_agent.py` |
| Continuous Learning | `learning_agent.py` |

Each inherits `BaseAgent`: `retrieve → ask → record`. Every decision lands in
`ai_decisions` with its rationale, confidence and eventual outcome.

### Workflows

| Graph | Nodes | Interrupts |
|---|---|---|
| `recording_graph` | start_recording → stop_recording → **keep_or_discard** → persist → reuse_scan → generate → compile | before `stop_recording` and `keep_or_discard` |
| `execution_graph` | preflight → execute → self_heal? → **teller_reset** → report → learn | none (runs to completion) |
| `brd_graph` | upload → analyse → **approval** → reuse_scan → apply_changes → compile → execute | before `approval` |

All three compile with a SQLite checkpointer (memory fallback), so an
interrupted workflow resumes from its last successful checkpoint —
`POST /api/execution/thread/{id}/resume`.

