## Section 12 — Self-healing

`backend/execution/self_healing.py :: heal()`

1. Promote the next-best locator from the ranked repository (free, no LLM).
2. Otherwise ask the Locator Agent for a replacement, grounded in the live DOM
   and the known locator list. Never invents an attribute absent from the DOM.
3. Apply if confidence ≥ `SELF_HEAL_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` — persist the new
   locator, demote the failed one, and patch the generated page object in place.
4. Between the two thresholds → human approval (Section 17).
5. Below `RERECORD_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` → flag for re-recording with the reason
   written into the report.

Every attempt is logged to `self_heal_log` with before/after locators — that log
drives the diff view in the report.

