## Section 17 — Human-in-the-loop

| Gate | Mechanism |
|---|---|
| Keep / Discard after recording | `recording_graph` interrupt + `POST /api/recorder/decide` |
| Approve BRD-driven changes | `brd_graph` interrupt + `POST /api/brd/thread/{id}/approve` (auto for low risk when `AUTO_APPROVE_LOW_RISK=true`) |
| Approve a low-confidence self-heal | `self_healing.heal()` returns `needs_approval`; surfaced on the Execute screen and in `approvals` |

---

## Section 18 — Extending the platform

To add a capability, add an **agent** (subclass `BaseAgent`, register it in
`backend/agents/__init__.py`) and wire it as a **node** in an existing graph, or
extend the **knowledge repository**. Do not add a standalone script.

The test: does the addition make the platform more autonomous over time? The
Continuous Learning Agent is the reference implementation of that principle — it
turns every outcome, good or bad, into knowledge that reduces future manual work.
